    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d426">

                <pb facs="0420" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg304"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.304 M28/52.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 347.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-06-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 27, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 941
                    of the 19th instant, in which you report that the President of Cuba has issued a
                    decree directing a special demonstration of sympathy for the sailors of the Navy
                    of the United States who lost their lives in the explosion on the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>.</p>
                <pb facs="0421" n="305" xml:id="pg305"/>
                <p>As suggested by yon, the Department desires you at the proper time to convey to
                    the Cuban Government an appropriate expression of the thanks of the Government
                    of the United States for this demonstration of sympathy.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
